, and the tariff list touched the yen: NZDJPY stays two-sided.|The franc's haven bid and the kiwi's risk-off pain keep NZDCHF close to bearish but not there.|Deeper risk-off met the kiwi's weakening line, putting NZDCAD's bullish call under pressure.|Monday's risk-on spark is gone, so CADJPY's bearish read is back on firmer ground.|The franc's haven bid returned in force, keeping CADCHF's bearish read on track.|Both havens landed on the US tariff list, so CHFJPY stays a stand-off.|Gold lost another 1–2% on hot core PCE, and XAUUSD's dollar condition is now half met.")
